WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.198 --> 00:00:03.198
(slow serene music)

00:00:04.341 --> 00:00:08.008
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.690
- Hi, my name's Brenda Cantrell
and I'm the brand ambassador

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.090
at Unclaimed Baggage Center.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.010
We kinda say you know, we're
an amusement park of shopping.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.360
You just, it's a fun thing to do,

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.440
it's a fun place to come

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.686
and it's, we're a lot of
fun people to be around.

00:00:44.686 --> 00:00:46.200
(upbeat music)

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.960
So Unclaimed Baggage Center
started almost 50 years ago

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.810
in a tiny town in Alabama.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.363
And now it's a national
tourism destination.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.140
And when people come in
they just truly never know

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.340
what they're gonna find.

00:00:56.371 --> 00:00:58.954
(upbeat music)

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.961
You can tell the people that
have never been here before

00:01:09.961 --> 00:01:12.340
when they just walk a
few steps into the store

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.763
and they just stop and
look around in amazement.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.763
They're shocked at the
sheer size of our building.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.990
It's over 40,000 square feet,
and we cover a city block.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:23.620
But we stock about 5 to 7,000 unique items

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.850
to our sales floor everyday.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.070
Some of the craziest
things that we have found

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.040
would of course top the list
is the live rattle snake.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.373
Mummified falcons we've had in the past,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.720
headdresses that are very old.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.330
Things that belonged to
celebrities at one point.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.270
Vacuum packed frogs in a suitcase.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.423
Probably take the cake.

00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:42.436
(frog croaks)

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.870
Another interesting thing
is the movie Labyrinth,

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.163
the character Hoggle,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.490
is actually in our showcase.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:50.210
There was only one made for that movie.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.060
And there's a cult following for that

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.140
and we have Hoggle here in our showcase.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.670
The found treasures are
really just a highlight

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.936
of your time here in the store.

00:01:57.936 --> 00:02:00.519
(upbeat music)

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.940
- So this is just our
unclaimed baggage experience.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.430
It's where a guest gets to
go through an unprocessed bag

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.143
only one person on staff
has seen the contents.

00:02:08.143 --> 00:02:10.640
They've just taken out
anything harmful, embarrassing

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.070
or dangerous, but other than that,

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:13.793
it is strictly an unprocessed bag.

00:02:13.864 --> 00:02:16.040
You're gonna choose to
trash it, give it away,

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.427
sell it or clean it.

00:02:17.427 --> 00:02:20.060
And we clean about 50,000 items a month,

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.510
which is more than the average laundromat

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.673
does in an entire year.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:23.523
- Wow.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.401
- Wow, that's intense.

00:02:25.401 --> 00:02:29.068
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.573
- [Woman] We sell pieces
that are $10,000 every week.

00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:39.416
- [Customer] Wow.

00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:41.843
- That's not uncommon for us
to sell something like that.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.593
- Can I touch it?

00:02:43.593 --> 00:02:44.467
- Yeah, you wanna put it on?

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:47.093
- $21,000 on my wrist right now.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.563
Who would leave this in a suitcase?

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.513
That's crazy.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.540
- The single most expensive item

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.267
that we've ever had on our sales floor

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:58.353
is a men's Presidential
latinum Rolex watch.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.380
We had it appraised and
it was valued at $64,000

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.590
and a gentleman bought it for $32,000.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.620
- But I'm like, can you imagine
not only being the person

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.170
that owns this, but the
person who like, forgot it?

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.820
It's just like, wow.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.423
That's goals.

00:03:12.756 --> 00:03:15.339
(upbeat music)

00:03:23.031 --> 00:03:25.020
- [Man] Oh it is a ab doer.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.996
- [Woman] Wait, so you're
supposed to sit like that on it?

00:03:26.996 --> 00:03:27.829
(man laughs)

00:03:27.829 --> 00:03:28.922
- I don't know.

00:03:28.922 --> 00:03:29.755
(laughs)

00:03:29.755 --> 00:03:31.292
That's probably part of the fun.

00:03:31.292 --> 00:03:34.709
(upbeat saxophone music)

00:03:35.428 --> 00:03:36.759
- [Woman] That's good.

00:03:36.759 --> 00:03:40.176
(upbeat saxophone music)

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:49.363
- Cha ching!

00:03:49.363 --> 00:03:50.615
(all laugh)

00:03:50.615 --> 00:03:52.148
- [Woman] Nailed it.

00:03:52.148 --> 00:03:55.565
(upbeat saxophone music)

